  "b6_reason": "Transposons replicate via an RNA intermediate and so can supply the complementary RNA that triggers RNA interference, i.e. gene silencing.",
  "b6_working": "RNAi silences a gene by double-stranded RNA pairing with and degrading its mRNA. The complementary RNA can come from RNA viruses or from mobile genetic elements (transposons). PCR needs primers and Taq polymerase, autoradiography needs a radiolabelled probe, and sequencing needs primers/terminators - none use transposons.",
